<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Melus of Bari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1020</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Melus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> nobleman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a> who led revolts against Byzantine rule in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. After a failed rising in 1009, he returned in 1017 with Norman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>, the first Normans to fight in the region, but was crushed by the catepan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-boioannes">Basil Boioannes</a> at Cannae in 1018. He died in exile at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a> in 1020.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/melus-of-bari.jpg" alt="Melus of Bari" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: “User:Henricus [Public domain]” · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cape_of_Melus_of_Bari.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
